# Helium patches Krypton does not apply.
#
# These restyle or restructure the browser window itself: toolbar, tab strip,
# location bar and omnibox views, app menu, frame and caption buttons, side
# panel, split view, bars and bubbles, and Helium's layouts. KryptonUI
# replaces that layer, and its host hooks patch Chromium's own code directly,
# so Krypton carries none of Helium's version of it and is not held back
# when Helium has to re-port it to a new Chromium.
#
# Everything else Helium does (privacy, services, settings and other WebUI
# pages, new tab page, importers, search, network, noise) is still applied.
# When the module is not active, the window is Chromium's own Views UI.
#
# Paths are relative to Helium's patches/ directory. build.py and
# tools/validate_series.py refuse an entry Helium no longer has.

